course: dictionary
lesson: 16167
title: Wrapped: many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word wrapped is a good example. «Dad wrapped my present in shiny paper.» Here wrapped means covered with paper folded around something.
explain: «She wrapped her arms around her mum.» Nothing is covered here. Wrapped means held tight by folding your arms around someone. Ask yourself: what is being wrapped, and why? The clues in the sentence tell you the meaning.
explain: «Tom was wrapped up in his book and did not hear the bell.» Wrapped up in means so busy with, or so interested in, something that you forget everything else. «It was freezing, so Mum said, "Wrap up warm!"» Here wrap up means dress warmly.
fact: Wrapped means covered with paper, cloth or plastic folded around something.
fact: Wrapped can also mean holding someone by folding your arms around them.
fact: «Wrapped up in» means very busy with, or very interested in, something.
fact: «Wrapped up» also means dressed warmly, so you can be wrapped up warm on a cold day.
fact: Wrapped is the past tense of wrap: wrap, wraps, wrapped, wrapping.
exercise: «The cut on my knee was wrapped in a clean bandage.» What does wrapped mean here? | Dressed warmly for winter | *Covered with a cloth folded around it | Holding something tightly with arms | Busy and very interested in something
exercise: Lily says, «Wrap up warm, it's freezing!» What does wrap up mean here? | Hug someone tightly | Run very fast | *Dress warmly | Fold paper around a present
exercise: «Sam was wrapped up in his drawing and didn't hear his name.» What does wrapped up in mean? | Cold and shivering | *Very busy with and very interested in | Holding his friend tightly | Covered with paper
test: «She wrapped her arms around her little brother.» What does wrapped mean here? | Finished and put away | *Held tight by folding her arms around | Dressed warmly | Covered with paper
test: «The sandwiches were wrapped in foil to keep them fresh.» Why were the sandwiches wrapped? | To make them heavier | To hide them from the dog | To make them look bigger | *To keep them fresh
exam: Which sentence uses wrapped to mean dressed warmly? | Tom was wrapped up in his game and ignored his lunch | The present was wrapped in blue paper | She wrapped her arms around her cat | *Dad told us to stay wrapped up warm in the snow
